Travel and Expense Policy — effective January 1, 2026
Training notice: Fictional training data — not for operational use
Core requirements
Receipts are required for expenses of $25 or more. Business purpose is required for every expense. The employee may not approve their own expense.
Limits
Domestic hotel limit is $275 per night before tax. Meals are limited to $90 per person per day. Airfare must be economy class unless the CFO pre-approves another class in writing. Alcohol is reimbursable only when itemized and associated with an approved client event.
Timing and exceptions
Expense reports must be submitted within 30 days after the transaction. Documented exceptions require Finance Director approval.
